(D2 — Discrepancy 2 repro: the manual explains the in-place retype as
 "the conversion that the corresponding static cast would use"
 (LANGUAGE.md:2642), but the corresponding static cast on a value
 (`v as a number`) is itself a compile error — the conversion the analogy
 references is not implemented for values (ROADMAP finding 21). The in-place
 statement form (VAL-09/VAL-10) works; the `as`-cast-on-value form does not.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D2.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Cannot cast v to a number: v's type is only known at runtime, and
   casting a dynamically-tagged value is not currently supported by the
   compiler (a known gap, not yet resolvable from within the language).
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a value called v is "357".
a number called n is v as a number.
print n.
